16.34. Relation of Jacobi's Zeta Function to the Theta Functions
Columns: \rho_{x}=\frac{\partial}{\partial u}\ln\Theta(u)\]
16.34.1    Z(u)=2K\frac{\pi}{\vartheta_{z}^{\ast}\left(\frac{\pi u}{2K}\right)}\frac{cn\ u\ dn\ u}{sn\ u}\]
16.34.2   \rho_{x}^{\ast}\left(\frac{\pi u}{2K}\right)\frac{dn\ u\ sn\ u}{cn\ u}\]
16.34.3   \rho_{x}^{\ast}\left(\frac{\pi u}{2K}\right)m\,\frac{sn\ u\ cn\ u}{dn\ u}\]
16.34.4   \rho_{x}^{\ast}\left(\frac{\pi u}{2K}\right)\frac{\pi}{\vartheta_{z}^{\ast}\left(\frac{\pi u}{2K}\right)}\]
16.35. Calculation of Jacobi's Zeta Function Z(u|m) by Use of the Arithmetic-Geometric Mean
Form the A.G.M. scale 17.6 starting with
16.35.1    a_0=1, b_0=\sqrtm_1, c_0=\sqrtm
terminating at the Nth step when c_N_ is negligible to the accuracy required. Find c_N_ in degrees where
16.35.2   \rho_{N}=2^{\alpha}\alpha_{N}u\frac{180^{\circ}}{\pi}\]
and then compute successively c_N-1, c_N-2, n, n, n from the recurrence relation
16.35.3   \sin\ (2\varphi_{n-1}-\varphi_{n})=\frac{c_n}{a_n}\sin\varphi_n.
Then
16.35.4
Z(u|m)=c_1\sin\varphi_1+c_2\sin\varphi_2+\dots+c_N\sin\varphi_N.
